WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.429 --> 00:00:05.180
There are some truly talented actors backing
up Oscar winner Brie Larson as Carol Danvers,

00:00:05.180 --> 00:00:09.330
most of whom you've probably seen on several
occasions without even knowing it.

00:00:09.330 --> 00:00:13.480
From her allies in Starforce to the villains
of the piece, here's why you recognize the

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:14.380
cast of Captain Marvel.

00:00:15.400 --> 00:00:20.160
Gemma Chan joins the Captain Marvel cast as
Minn-Erva, a Kree scientist and loyalist.

00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:24.720
In the comics, she was part of a plot to eliminate
90 percent of the Kree empire, which would

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:27.880
have forced the remaining 10 percent to evolve
at a quicker rate.

00:00:27.880 --> 00:00:32.180
Chan turned down a job with an international
law firm to pursue a career in acting, which

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:36.710
began in earnest when she was cast in the
critically acclaimed sci-fi series Humans.

00:00:36.710 --> 00:00:40.870
She then scored a variety of minor roles in
Hollywood, but Tinseltown didn't really start

00:00:40.870 --> 00:00:45.000
paying attention to Chan until 2018's Crazy
Rich Asians blew up.

00:00:46.010 --> 00:00:49.960
In the comics, Minn-Erva worked closely with
fellow Starforce member Att-Lass.

00:00:49.960 --> 00:00:54.239
When he discovered that she wanted to eradicate
the vast majority of their race, he intentionally

00:00:54.239 --> 00:00:57.420
made his suit self destruct, taking Minn-Erva
with him.

00:00:57.420 --> 00:01:01.739
Att-Lass is played by Algenis Pérez Soto,
a relatively inexperienced actor with only

00:01:01.739 --> 00:01:03.610
a few film credits to his name.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:08.390
One of those films was helmed by Anna Boden
and Ryan Fleck, co-directors of Captain Marvel.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:13.070
They've known Soto for a long time, having
plucked him from obscurity to star in their

00:01:13.070 --> 00:01:15.180
2008 baseball drama, Sugar.

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:19.830
He fell off the radar following Sugar, but
in 2017 Soto made an unexpected return to

00:01:19.830 --> 00:01:22.400
film with Dominican boxing drama Samba.

00:01:23.480 --> 00:01:27.110
When Rune Temte confirmed that he was going
to be appearing in Captain Marvel, he could

00:01:27.110 --> 00:01:28.420
barely contain his excitement.

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:35.860
The actor was quite clearly fired up for his
Marvel debut, but what does his character

00:01:35.860 --> 00:01:36.860
have to offer?

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:38.380
Well, he's fairly minor.

00:01:38.380 --> 00:01:42.760
You can count Bron-Char's total comics appearances
on one hand, though he belongs to a small

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.770
group of Marvel characters who've been able
to destroy one of Captain America's shields

00:01:46.770 --> 00:01:48.121
in battle, so he's no pushover.

00:01:48.121 --> 00:01:53.040
If you've ever watched Temte in The Last Kingdom,
you'll know that the big Norwegian is already

00:01:53.040 --> 00:01:54.970
well-versed in battle sequences.

00:01:54.970 --> 00:01:59.409
He's best known for playing bearded warlord
Ubba in the historical fiction series, for

00:01:59.409 --> 00:02:01.899
which he trained in ancient viking martial
arts.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:07.000
Temte has also been seen in Sky Atlantic's
Fortitude and sports biopic Eddie The Eagle.

00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:12.790
Marvel fans will no doubt recognize Djimon
Hounsou from his supporting role in 2014's

00:02:12.790 --> 00:02:14.420
Guardians of the Galaxy.

00:02:14.420 --> 00:02:18.820
He plays the MCU incarnation of Korath-Thak,
also known as Korath the Pursuer.

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:23.500
In the comics, he was a cyber-geneticist charged
with engineering cybernetic warriors for the

00:02:23.500 --> 00:02:24.460
Kree military.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:28.939
He wound up using the tech that he invented
on himself, gaining powers in the process.

00:02:28.939 --> 00:02:33.449
Hounsou made his breakthrough in Steven Spielberg's
Amistad, but he's perhaps best known for his

00:02:33.449 --> 00:02:38.020
turn as Juba in Ridley Scott's Gladiator,
providing a foil for leading man Russell Crowe.

00:02:38.460 --> 00:02:42.430
The Benin-born actor went on to work with
some of the industry's biggest names, including

00:02:42.430 --> 00:02:47.040
Angelina Jolie in Lara Croft: Tomb Raider
– The Cradle of Life, Leonardo DiCaprio

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:50.299
in Blood Diamond, and Keanu Reeves in Constantine.

00:02:50.320 --> 00:02:54.060
What many people don't know is that he actually
beat Chadwick Boseman to the part of King

00:02:54.060 --> 00:02:59.640
T'Challa — Hounsou voiced the Wakandan leader
in BET's six-part animated Black Panther series.

00:02:59.740 --> 00:03:04.840
When he spoke to Slashfilm at a February 2019
presser, Hounsou revealed that Captain Marvel

00:03:04.840 --> 00:03:07.760
isn't closely connected to Guardians of the
Galaxy, saying:

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:12.900
"This is a completely separate story, standalone
story, nothing to do with Guardians other

00:03:12.900 --> 00:03:16.140
than the fact that some of those characters
interact with each other later."

00:03:16.140 --> 00:03:17.760
Speaking of some of those characters...

00:03:18.520 --> 00:03:22.980
Another dead Guardians of the Galaxy character
who pops up in the '90s-set Captain Marvel

00:03:22.989 --> 00:03:26.400
is Kree zealot Ronan the Accuser, played by
Lee Pace.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:28.480
"WHAT are you doing?!"

00:03:29.020 --> 00:03:32.400
"I’m distracting you, ya big turd blossom!”

00:03:32.900 --> 00:03:36.820
According to Pace, we're going to see a slightly
more chilled-out version of Ronan.

00:03:36.829 --> 00:03:37.849
The actor explained:

00:03:37.849 --> 00:03:41.780
"This isn't the same Ronan that we saw in
Guardians of the Galaxy, this is before he's

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:44.159
become a fundamentalist about the Kree way
of living.

00:03:44.159 --> 00:03:45.559
But he's still true Kree."

00:03:45.559 --> 00:03:49.890
The opportunity to reprise the role of Ronan
was welcomed by Pace, who thoroughly enjoyed

00:03:49.890 --> 00:03:50.900
working on Guardians.

00:03:50.900 --> 00:03:51.900
He told IGN:

00:03:51.900 --> 00:03:53.069
"I loved that film.

00:03:53.069 --> 00:03:58.029
I found the character very, very interesting…
this kind of charismatic space terrorist."

00:03:58.029 --> 00:04:02.119
For most actors, "space terrorist" would be
the weirdest role on their résumé by some

00:04:02.119 --> 00:04:06.489
distance, but Pace was both a vampire and
an elf before he was a Kree — the actor

00:04:06.489 --> 00:04:10.610
played Garrett in the final installment of
the Twilight franchise and appeared in every

00:04:10.610 --> 00:04:15.170
film in Peter Jackson's Hobbit trilogy as
Thranduil, the Elven king of the Woodland

00:04:15.170 --> 00:04:15.880
Realm.

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:19.960
"Why did you do that?

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:21.440
You promised to set him free.”

00:04:22.200 --> 00:04:22.900
“… And I did."

00:04:23.500 --> 00:04:27.400
The identity of Jude Law's character was one
of the biggest mysteries surrounding Captain

00:04:27.409 --> 00:04:29.129
Marvel during its production.

00:04:29.129 --> 00:04:33.530
The studio seemingly confirmed that the British
actor was playing Mar-Vell, the original Captain

00:04:33.530 --> 00:04:38.620
Marvel in the comics, in December 2018, but
a few months later it was revealed that Law

00:04:38.620 --> 00:04:39.939
was actually playing Yon-Rogg.

00:04:39.939 --> 00:04:44.360
He had to wear colored contact lenses to play
the Kree commander, but most film fans will

00:04:44.360 --> 00:04:47.729
still have recognized Law from his many Hollywood
roles over the years.

00:04:47.729 --> 00:04:51.789
He came to the attention of international
audiences at the turn of millennium the when

00:04:51.789 --> 00:04:56.900
he starred alongside Matt Damon and a number
of other big names in The Talented Mr. Ripley.

00:04:56.900 --> 00:05:01.729
Law went on to work with many of the industry's
top directors, and in 2018, he took on the

00:05:01.729 --> 00:05:06.740
iconic role of Albus Dumbledore in Fantastic
Beasts: The Crimes of Grindelwald, playing

00:05:06.740 --> 00:05:09.400
a younger version of the future Hogwarts headmaster.

00:05:09.400 --> 00:05:13.169
It appears as though Captain Marvel was the
most physically demanding role that Law has

00:05:13.169 --> 00:05:14.160
taken in a long while.

00:05:14.520 --> 00:05:18.680
When Slashfilm asked him how many action sequences
he had in the movie, the actor confirmed that

00:05:18.680 --> 00:05:20.120
there were three in total, saying:

00:05:20.139 --> 00:05:23.060
"One of them's been really fun, which we already
shot.

00:05:23.060 --> 00:05:25.200
There are some other fantastic battle sequences."

00:05:26.180 --> 00:05:30.810
Brie Larson officially arrived on the Hollywood
A-list with 2015's Room, putting in an Oscar-winning

00:05:30.810 --> 00:05:33.680
performance as a woman held captive for seven
years.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:37.310
Everyone knew her name after the Academy named
her Best Actress, but people already knew

00:05:37.310 --> 00:05:38.310
her face.

00:05:38.310 --> 00:05:42.620
Before her star-making turn as Joy Newsome,
Larson was becoming one of those actors that

00:05:42.620 --> 00:05:46.639
you're sure you've seen somewhere before,
even if you can't put your finger on it.

00:05:46.639 --> 00:05:50.629
After some scene-stealing roles in comedy
hits like Scott Pilgrim vs. the World and

00:05:50.629 --> 00:05:55.040
the reboot of 21 Jump Street, she made waves
on the indie scene with a powerful performance

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.409
in Short Term 12.

00:05:56.409 --> 00:06:00.840
She worked with Mark Wahlberg in The Gambler
and supported Amy Schumer in Trainwreck, but

00:06:00.840 --> 00:06:04.720
as soon as she laid her hands on that coveted
statuette, bigger offers started to come her

00:06:04.740 --> 00:06:05.260
way.

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:10.760
After Room, Larson booked the co-lead in Kong:
Skull Island, playing an anti-war photojournalist.

00:06:10.900 --> 00:06:15.120
In Kong, she got to work with Marvel veteran
Samuel L. Jackson, who plays a major role

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.360
in Captain Marvel.

00:06:16.360 --> 00:06:20.940
Larson also cast Jackson in her feature directorial
debut, Unicorn Store.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.040
After their years of collaborating, Jackson
has confirmed that Larson's fitness regimen

00:06:25.040 --> 00:06:28.960
for Skull Island was nowhere near as strenuous
as what she's been doing to get in shape for

00:06:28.960 --> 00:06:31.060
her big MCU debut.

00:06:31.300 --> 00:06:32.500
Jackson told Collider:

00:06:32.660 --> 00:06:36.440
"The girl that I did Kong and Unicorn Store
with is not this person.

00:06:36.440 --> 00:06:38.140
She's like five percent body fat now."

00:06:39.080 --> 00:06:43.610
The supremely talented Ben Mendelsohn seemed
to appear from out of nowhere, but the Australian

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:46.960
has quietly been putting in outstanding performances
for years now.

00:06:46.960 --> 00:06:50.800
He came to the attention of international
audiences with his starring role in the Aussie

00:06:50.800 --> 00:06:55.960
drama Animal Kingdom, a Melbourne-set crime
flick that wowed critics the world over.

00:06:55.960 --> 00:07:00.250
The movie was his Hollywood calling card,
and in recent years the character actor has

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:02.340
become Tinseltown's new go-to villain.

00:07:02.340 --> 00:07:06.259
You'll probably recognize Mendelsohn from
his turn as Imperial Military director Orson

00:07:06.259 --> 00:07:11.939
Krennic in 2016's Rogue One: A Star Wars Story,
or perhaps you’ve seen him in 2018's Ready

00:07:11.939 --> 00:07:12.939
Player One.

00:07:12.939 --> 00:07:17.970
He played Nolan Sorrento, CEO of the shady
company seeking full control over the movie's

00:07:17.970 --> 00:07:20.440
virtual reality haven, the OASIS.

00:07:20.440 --> 00:07:24.600
He's gained a reputation as something of a
chameleon, a description that just so happens

00:07:24.650 --> 00:07:27.220
to fit his Captain Marvel character perfectly.

00:07:27.230 --> 00:07:31.699
The Emmy-winner plays shape-shifting villain
Talos in the twenty-first MCU movie.

00:07:31.699 --> 00:07:35.939
Mendelsohn explained a little about the Skrulls
in typical comical fashion when he spoke to

00:07:35.939 --> 00:07:38.040
reporters during a set visit.

00:07:38.040 --> 00:07:41.080
“Space pigs, you know what I mean.

00:07:41.080 --> 00:07:42.389
Like, tough, tough.

00:07:42.389 --> 00:07:44.139
Big sort of *snort*...

00:07:44.140 --> 00:07:45.180
Big tough Skrulls."

00:07:45.740 --> 00:07:49.831
Captain Marvel is undoubtedly the biggest
gig of Lashana Lynch's career to date, but

00:07:49.831 --> 00:07:52.349
the English actress isn't exactly a newcomer.

00:07:52.349 --> 00:07:56.400
If you watch a lot of British TV, there's
a good chance you've seen Lynch before.

00:07:56.400 --> 00:08:01.500
She appeared in everything from police procedurals
and crime dramas to murder mysteries and adventure

00:08:01.500 --> 00:08:04.280
fantasies while earning her stripes in the
UK.

00:08:04.280 --> 00:08:09.650
In 2016, her hard work was rewarded when she
won the lead role in ABC's Still Star-Crossed.

00:08:09.650 --> 00:08:15.029
The show is a sequel to Romeo &amp; Juliet, taking
place after the events of Shakespeare's tragedy.

00:08:15.029 --> 00:08:17.169
Sadly for Lynch, it wasn't well-received.

00:08:17.169 --> 00:08:21.300
Still Star-Crossed received middling reviews,
and the ratings were not good.

00:08:21.300 --> 00:08:25.879
ABC shifted the show from its primetime slot
and later canceled it altogether, scrapping

00:08:25.879 --> 00:08:27.599
a planned second season.

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:31.229
Lynch was given the chance to bounce back
with Captain Marvel, in which she plays Carol

00:08:31.229 --> 00:08:33.570
Danvers' Air Force buddy, Maria Rambeau.

00:08:33.570 --> 00:08:38.010
She was a minor character in the comics, but
the MCU version will be far more important

00:08:38.010 --> 00:08:39.040
to the titular hero.

00:08:40.010 --> 00:08:44.280
If you don't recognize Samuel L. Jackson,
you must have avoided movies your entire life.

00:08:44.280 --> 00:08:48.080
From cult classics to tentpole blockbusters,
Jackson has been around the block more than

00:08:48.080 --> 00:08:51.920
a few times, becoming Hollywood's most bankable
star in the process.

00:08:57.120 --> 00:08:57.860
"Ahhhh."

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:02.400
His face is one that the majority of Americans
would know in an instant, but his physical

00:09:02.410 --> 00:09:06.620
appearance in Captain Marvel is likely to
confuse anyone unfamiliar with the setting

00:09:06.620 --> 00:09:07.620
of the movie.

00:09:07.620 --> 00:09:11.720
Of course, since Captain Marvel is set in
the 1990s, Jackson has been de-aged a few

00:09:11.720 --> 00:09:14.290
decades by the special effects wizards at
Lola VFX.

00:09:14.290 --> 00:09:18.960
It's a technique that Marvel has been experimenting
with in recent years, but Captain Marvel is

00:09:18.960 --> 00:09:22.120
the first time it's been used for the entirety
of a movie.

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.389
Jackson gave the technique his full approval
on his official Instagram account, posting

00:09:25.389 --> 00:09:28.649
a photo of himself as the young Nick Fury
along with the caption:

00:09:28.649 --> 00:09:31.650
"Wow, this Marvel de-aging thing is doper
than I thought!"

00:09:31.650 --> 00:09:34.180
The '90s setting means fans will get to see
the S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:09:34.180 --> 00:09:38.649
boss minus his famous eye patch, though judging
from some of Jackson's recent comments, he'll

00:09:38.649 --> 00:09:41.300
be down to one eye again by the time the credits
roll.

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.260
"How does Fury even see these?”

00:09:45.940 --> 00:09:46.460
“He turns.”

00:09:47.020 --> 00:09:47.680
“Sounds exhausting."

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:53.480
Clark Gregg's Phil Coulson is a rookie agent
during the time Captain Marvel is set.

00:09:53.480 --> 00:09:57.250
Speaking to Den of Geek, Gregg revealed that
the S.H.I.E.L.D stalwart will be a total newbie

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:58.990
when he meets Carol Danvers, saying:

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:00.709
"He's a bit of a new guy in S.H.I.E.L.D.

00:10:00.709 --> 00:10:01.899
He's a lot younger.

00:10:01.899 --> 00:10:06.130
It's the earliest we will have seen him, so
when he says, 'Mr. Stark, this isn't my first

00:10:06.130 --> 00:10:09.540
rodeo' in Iron Man, this is maybe the rodeo
he's talking about."

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:14.240
Gregg managed to book minor movie parts throughout
the '90s, later finding a home on TV.

00:10:14.240 --> 00:10:18.060
After landing one-off parts in Sex and the
City and other shows, Gregg joined the cast

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:23.790
of The West Wing, sporadically appearing as
FBI Special Agent Michael Casper between 2001

00:10:23.790 --> 00:10:25.070
and 2004.

00:10:25.070 --> 00:10:29.730
In 2008, he directed and acted in Choke, an
adaptation of Chuck Palahniuk's book of the

00:10:29.730 --> 00:10:30.990
same name.

00:10:30.990 --> 00:10:35.670
Ancient, all-knowing, and a big green floating
head, the Supreme Intelligence is a collection

00:10:35.670 --> 00:10:40.269
of the smartest Kree minds, merged over a
million years in the past to create the ultimate

00:10:40.269 --> 00:10:41.870
weapon to defeat the Skrulls.

00:10:41.870 --> 00:10:45.130
Who better to step into that role than acclaimed
actress Annette Bening?

00:10:45.130 --> 00:10:49.800
Bening has been acting steadily since the
late '80s, appearing in everything from American

00:10:49.800 --> 00:10:53.329
Beauty to Tim Burton's cult classic comedy
Mars Attacks.

00:10:53.329 --> 00:10:58.040
More recently, she was nominated for an Oscar
for her leading role in The Kids Are Alright.

00:10:58.040 --> 00:11:01.880
Fans got a glimpse of Bening as the ancient
megamind in a recent Captain Marvel trailer.

00:11:01.880 --> 00:11:06.149
Although there are some differences in her
appearance -- she has a body, for one -- it's

00:11:06.149 --> 00:11:08.910
clear that this acting powerhouse is a good
fit for the role.

00:11:08.910 --> 00:11:12.649
But even the Supreme Intelligence needs a
little help from time to time, and Bening

00:11:12.649 --> 00:11:16.889
had to turn to an unlikely source to explain
some of the more convoluted aspects of Captain

00:11:16.889 --> 00:11:18.220
Marvel to her.

00:11:18.220 --> 00:11:25.060
"My kids, whom I then told the story to and
asked them to please explain to me what the

00:11:25.060 --> 00:11:26.780
hell was going on!”

00:11:26.900 --> 00:11:29.100
Check out one of our newest videos right here!

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:32.860
Plus, even more Looper videos about your favorite
movies are coming soon.

00:11:32.860 --> 00:11:36.730
Subscribe to our YouTube channel and hit the
bell so you don't miss a single one.

